      "observations": [
        "All owned searchWidgets.js hunks were read with the full findTemplates loop and its hideInvalidActions consumer. The try block covers both obtaining msgDatabase and invoking enumerateMessages, not later iteration through returned headers. enumerator is reset to null for each identity; a caught access exception logs a URI and message, then the existing falsy guard continues to the next identity. A folder is added to foldersScanned before access, so another identity using the same folder does not retry it in this scan. Successful other folders still contribute template labels/URIs.",
        "The owning action menu hides Reply with Template when the returned list is empty. The patch avoids this particular database-access exception escaping from that scan; folder lookup, header iteration and field access outside the try remain fallible. No database repair, broad error suppression, UI reproduction or new test is established.",
        "Full primary2023919 description/comments0–2 and activity/footer, plus D288195 creation-to-final and its two actual author/reviewer inline bodies, were read from retained originals. The URI suggestion is adopted; logging the complete error as a second console.warn argument is explicitly declined by the author and is absent from source. The initial reviewer could not reproduce corruption, and later asks for a new Try because old output was unavailable. Linked job bodies and screenshot were not inspected; remote-completion reports are historical only.",
        "Manual style checks preserve the narrow catch and existing early continue, concrete URI in the warning and local array-producing loop. The adopted logging choice is scoped to this diagnostic, not a global ban on logging error objects. No tests, assertions or accessibility controls change."
      ],
