      "observations": [
        "All17owned paths and changed Fluent/markup/module hunks were read. Exposed account, chat, calendar and address-book creation labels change New to Add and related title/description IDs are wired together. The unified-toolbar item keeps id create-address-book, templateId createAddressBookTemplate and required module identity while labelId and template label-id/data-l10n-id change. Command IDs and popup dispatch are unchanged. This is a wording/resource migration, not a new account or address-book creation operation.",
        "The actual CreateAddressBookButton extends UnifiedToolbarButton and forwards popup data-command to goDoCommand. The base label consumer calls document.l10n.setAttributes on its inner label for label-id; the template separately localizes the button title. Matching visible-label and title resources are checked in accepted source. All exposed controls were checked statically; no localized rendering, access-key collision, keyboard, focus or screen-reader result is inferred.",
        "Full primary1993849 current description/comments0–7 and activity/footer, plus sparse D294826 creation-to-close timeline, were read from originals. The report distinguishes adding an existing mailbox from creating one. Discussion allows the traditional New submenu while objecting to New Account wording in App Menu; this does not establish a repository-wide ban on New. A reviewer asks about titles saying Create new, then a source update and later approval occur. The owned labels/titles show the actual result; approval alone is not the adoption proof. There are no submitted inline or summary-history bodies. Try request/link and remote completions are historical, not a run here.",
