      "sourceAnalysis": [
        "All367owned diff lines in the component and browser test were read. The patch caches fullName/unreadCount/totalCount/formatted folderSize in private fields instead of reading counts from label text, uses equality guards and reuses an existing Text node for count/size updates. The actual tree observer requests subtree childList, not characterData, and its callback rebuilds row data. The fallback element.textContent assignment can still create a child-list mutation when no suitable text node exists; this is not a claim that every update bypasses the observer or a measured speedup.",
        "The50ms scheduler clears the prior timeout and starts a new one. Each actual #updateAriaLabel invocation increments a serial; allSettled uses only fulfilled strings, then applies aria-label and title only if that invocation is still newest. The serial changes when localization work starts, not when a setter merely schedules the next timeout. An older result can therefore still apply during that interval; no stronger immediate invalidation guarantee is inferred from the JSDoc. The code neither cancels Fluent promises nor resets the timeout field after firing. Selected callers set formatted folder size via formatFolderSize and counts via folder getters.",
        "The new test checks label substrings after synchronous50/51/52 writes, then100/200 writes separated by60ms, and final restoration. It uses four fixed500ms waits with explicit lint exceptions. It does not hold/release localization promises, assert request counts or observe every intermediate label; absence of50at the final read does not prove it was never processed. The overlap comment acknowledges uncertainty. All five added assertion messages are nonempty; one lacks should, a writing preference rather than a defect by itself. No test ran.",
        "Full primary2004961 current description/comments0–14 and activity/footer were read. The early zero-unread hypothesis is challenged by the reporter, and the reviewer acknowledges uncertainty. The author and reporter distinguish visible badges from stale tooltip/ARIA name. Reports of compacting and promise ordering remain hypotheses. Initial landing, backout for potential mac test failures, proposed dependency1962967 fix and later reland are distinct; linked jobs/dependency bodies were not expanded and no causal cure is inferred.",
        "Full D293620 creation-to-final timeline, all seven actual submitted old/resolved/current inline bodies, literal serial replacement and both Old/New summary bodies were read. Source adopts serial tracking in place of the proposed AbortController, fixed test waits and documentation of formatFolderSize, observer cost/parameters and private-field types. The reviewer explicitly says elapsed55ms cannot prove localization is still pending and suggests controlled settlement; this test does not add it. Done and approval are checked against source, not treated as adoption. Historical build results are separate from fresh validation.",
        "Accepted later count/size setters separate equality-based text changes from persisted visibility. Existing supported visibility lesson11f34db… owns that later contract; the original early-return setters here do not receive it. Existing focused comment/type/scheduler lessons are reused rather than repeated. Comments that say properties changing immediately invalidates old results are broader than the actual timer-stage serial contract. No global fixed-delay exception or source-comment policy is learned."
